Z||000000||87GTZ34||12-27-2001||12:22 PM||||This doesn't look like new news but I haven't seen anything posted on it.  Did you know that GM has a twin turbo N* offering.  It appears that it is only available in Europe so if anyone has friends or relatives that are gearheads...<P>here's the link  <A HREF="http://www.gm.com/cgi-bin/pr_display.pl?1441" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gm.com/cgi-bin/pr_display.pl?1441</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||12-27-2001||12:51 PM||||I don't think you could get that in a production car. Somewhere I have a picture of one on a stand. I'll look for it.<P>But.........I could be happy with it!||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||12-27-2001||06:58 PM||||That's the race-only motor in the Caddilac LMP Le Mans car   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.mulsannescorner.com/motor_galpop_01.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.mulsannescorner.com/motor_galpop_02.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.mulsannescorner.com/motor_galpop_04.jpg"> <P>I belive this is the LMP Motor:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.mobilonline.com/mobil/galeri/konsep/images/ksp_cadillacns2.jpg"> <P><BR>No, you can't get an Eldorado with one (yet   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> but it does show you just how close to a preped race motor the Northstar really is. (stock block and bearings and heads are used on the LMP. Crank/rods/springs/lifters get changed out, and it actually is *de* stroked   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Roumour has it that it puts out well over the 580bhp they claim.  Especially this year with the 180degree crank.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by artherd (edited 12-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||12-27-2001||07:27 PM||||<BR>Here's a great source for 'hot' Northstar parts:  <A HREF="http://www.chrfab.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.chrfab.com/</A> <P>They have built and dynoed a production Turbo Northstar V8 making 800bhp. (no restrictors like in Le Mans.)<P>Here's a pic of theirs:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.chrfab.com/images/CHRF%20Images/MVC-876S.JPG"> <P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">      <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red.                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver, In-Progreess.                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000004||Leper||12-27-2001||08:10 PM||||I bet the LMP motor sounds better though.||||reg||1
Z||000005||artherd||12-27-2001||11:44 PM||||With an 180degree crank (which Chrafb does offer, though I do not belive is used on that Turbo motor...)  the LMP motor darned ought to sound better  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>You can get scary-close to that motor with their parts however.<P>(PS: those 'hemi' looking valve covers are kind of a 'classic' hot-rodder's thing.  Make the 4-cam engine look a little more retro.  Cool in a '32 ford, but not my thing for a mondern supercar. Easy enough to change 'em though!)<P>This will probally sound cool at around 8500 or so (I hope!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/northstar/2/nstar-front-on.jpg"> <P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Leper:<BR><B>I bet the LMP motor sounds better though.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">      <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red.                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver, In-Progreess.                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
